{% doc %}
  Maps — public parent block (Composite / orchestrator).

  A Google map with an overlaid card: a `<select>` of branches plus the selected branch's own panel.
  Branch data lives in this block's OWN nested `_maps-location` children, and each branch's panel
  content is composed from ITS nested blocks in turn (three levels: maps → _maps-location → text).
  A parent block cannot read a nested block's settings, so each child renders TWO fragments
  around a "maps/split" HTML marker comment; this block captures `content_for 'blocks'`, splits
  on the marker and routes each half (the `<option>`s into the dropdown, the panels into the card) —
  the same pattern as `blocks/_tab.liquid` + `sections/tabs.liquid`.

  The map URL is composed in JS, never in Liquid: the child owns `map_query` while the parent owns the
  API key / zoom / map type, and neither can read the other. The map is always deferred to viewport
  entry, so there is never a server-rendered iframe (no-JS = card + dropdown, no map).

  @example
  {% content_for 'block', type: 'maps', id: 'maps' %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign settings = block.settings

  assign color_scheme = settings.color_scheme
  if settings.inherit_color_scheme
    assign color_scheme = ''
  endif

  comment
    Fold border_opacity into a custom border_color so BOTH settings apply together
    (border-style only applies opacity to the scheme border color, not a custom one).
  endcomment
  assign border_alpha = settings.border_opacity | default: 100 | divided_by: 100.0
-%}

{%- capture children -%}
  {% content_for 'blocks' %}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- liquid
  comment
    Split-marker routing. Every `_maps-location` emits
      <!-- @maps/split -->OPTION<!-- @maps/split -->PANEL
    so the concatenated capture starts with a marker and then alternates option / panel:
    index0 0 = "" (the empty head), 1 = option, 2 = panel, 3 = option, …
  endcomment
  assign parts = children | strip | split: '<!-- @maps/split -->'
  assign options_html = ''
  assign panels_html = ''
  assign item_count = 0

  for part in parts
    assign is_option = forloop.index0 | modulo: 2
    if is_option == 1
      assign options_html = options_html | append: part
      assign item_count = item_count | plus: 1
    else
      comment
        A nested block cannot resolve its own index, so every child ships `hidden="hidden"` and the
        FIRST panel routed here has that exact token stripped — one panel is visible before JS runs.
        The token is a string contract with `blocks/_maps-location.liquid`; keep it unbroken.

        `panel` is a MUST, not a style choice: `assign` writes to the outermost scope while `for`
        binds `part` in the loop's own inner scope, so `assign part = …` here would never be seen by
        the `append` below (lookup is innermost-first) and the strip would silently do nothing.
        `panels_html == blank` is also deliberate: parts[0] is the empty head, and appending it
        leaves `panels_html` blank, so the guard still fires on the first REAL panel.
      endcomment
      assign panel = part
      if panels_html == blank
        assign panel = panel | replace_first: 'hidden="hidden"', ''
      endif
      assign panels_html = panels_html | append: panel
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    ONE rule covers both ways the card can go: it renders only if the merchant left `show_card` on
    AND there is at least one Location to put in it. With zero locations the card would be empty
    anyway (no dropdown, no panel), so it is dropped and the block renders as a clean standalone map.
  endcomment
  assign render_card = false
  if settings.show_card and item_count > 0
    assign render_card = true
  endif

  comment
    The map query must NEVER resolve to blank. When the card renders, JS reads the active branch from
    the `<select>`; when it does not, there is no select to read, so the parent resolves the query
    itself and hands it over as `data-fallback-query`. Three tiers, in order:

      1. the FIRST location's own query — this is the `show_card: false` + locations case, where the
         dropdown is gone but the locations are not, so the map stays on location one. A parent
         cannot read a nested block's settings, so the value is parsed back out of the captured
         `<option>` markup; that markup is this file's own contract with `_maps-location`.
      2. the shop's own address, composed BY HAND. Deliberately NOT `shop.address.summary`: that is
         documented as including the first and last NAME and omitting the zip — a person's name in a
         geographic query is worse than no query at all.
      3. `maps_demo_query` below — the SAME literal the preset ships, so this block has one demo
         address, not two. On a store with no address configured this shows Los Angeles, which is not
         the merchant's shop; an obviously-placeholder map still beats an empty hole, and the Theme
         Editor hint keeps nudging them to add a real location.

    `fallback_query` / `fallback_title` come out HTML-ESCAPED, ready to print straight into an
    attribute. Tier 1 arrives already escaped (the child escaped it on the way in), so only the
    tier-2/3 values are piped through `escape` — do NOT add a second `escape` at the output site.
  endcomment
  assign maps_demo_query = '6100 Wilshire Blvd, Los Angeles'
  assign fallback_query = ''
  assign fallback_title = ''

  unless render_card
    if options_html != blank
      assign query_parts = options_html | split: 'data-map-query="'
      if query_parts.size > 1
        assign fallback_query = query_parts[1] | split: '"' | first
      endif
      assign title_parts = options_html | split: 'data-map-title="'
      if title_parts.size > 1
        assign fallback_title = title_parts[1] | split: '"' | first
      endif
    endif

    if fallback_query == blank
      assign shop_query = ''
      if shop.address.street != blank
        assign shop_query = shop_query | append: shop.address.street | append: ', '
      endif
      if shop.address.city != blank
        assign shop_query = shop_query | append: shop.address.city | append: ', '
      endif
      if shop.address.province != blank
        assign shop_query = shop_query | append: shop.address.province | append: ', '
      endif
      if shop.address.zip != blank
        assign shop_query = shop_query | append: shop.address.zip | append: ', '
      endif
      if shop.address.country != blank
        assign shop_query = shop_query | append: shop.address.country | append: ', '
      endif
      assign shop_query = shop_query | remove_last: ', ' | strip
      if shop_query == blank
        assign shop_query = maps_demo_query
      endif
      assign fallback_query = shop_query | escape
    endif

    if fallback_title == blank
      if shop.name != blank
        assign fallback_title = 'blocks.maps.map_title' | t: name: shop.name
      else
        assign fallback_title = 'blocks.maps.map_title_fallback' | t
      endif
      assign fallback_title = fallback_title | escape
    endif
  endunless
-%}

{%- capture block_style -%}
  {% render 'spacing-style', settings: settings %}
  {% render 'size-style', settings: settings %}
  {% render 'border-style', settings: settings, use_mask_clip: false %}
  {%- comment -%}
    Card-only vars, emitted only when the card is actually rendered — `--f-row-gap*` is read by
    `.maps__panel`, `--maps-card-offset` / `--maps-card-width` by `.maps__card`, and all three live
    inside the card. With `show_card` off there is nothing left to read them.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if render_card -%}
    {% render 'gap-style',
      row_gap: settings.card_gap,
      row_gap_mobile: settings.card_gap_mobile,
      column_gap: 0,
      column_gap_mobile: 0
    %}
    --maps-card-offset: {{ settings.card_offset }}px;
    --maps-card-width: {{ settings.card_width }}px;
  {%- endif -%}
  {% render 'clamp-calculate-style',
    property_name: 'maps-map-height',
    min_value: settings.height_mobile,
    max_value: settings.height
  %}
  {%- if settings.border == 'solid' and settings.border_color != blank -%}
    --border-color: {{ settings.border_color | color_modify: 'alpha', border_alpha }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    The block picker renders the block inside a zero-width container; without a floor it measures 0×0.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if request.visual_preview_mode -%}
    min-width: 600px;
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Rendered unconditionally: since the query always resolves (three tiers above), a block with no
  Location child is still a working map rather than nothing at all.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script src="{{ 'maps.js' | asset_url }}" type="module" fetchpriority="low"></script>
{%- render 'maps-markup',
  settings: settings,
  options_html: options_html,
  panels_html: panels_html,
  item_count: item_count,
  render_card: render_card,
  fallback_query: fallback_query,
  fallback_title: fallback_title,
  block_id: block.id,
  color_scheme: color_scheme,
  block_style: block_style,
  shopify_attributes: block.shopify_attributes
-%}

{% schema %}
